      "id": "wa36vrl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Heat"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Heat is a form of energy that flows from a body at a higher temperature to a body at a lower temperature.",
        "Temperature is the measure of the degree of hotness or coldness of a body, measured using Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin scales.",
        "Heat transfer occurs through three primary mechanisms: Conduction, Convection, and Radiation.",
        "Thermal expansion is the tendency of matter to change in shape, area, and volume in response to a change in temperature."
      ],
      "id": "p1wzbhq"
